        "title": "Civil Liberties: ACLU, Frankfurter, Thurgood Marshall, Ruth Bader Ginsburg",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TIMELINE OF CIVIL LIBERTIES EXPANSION:\n  1919  ACLU founded (from National Civil Liberties Bureau)\n  1925  Gitlow v. New York: 1st Amendment incorporated to states\n        (14th Amendment applies Bill of Rights to states)\n  1931  Near v. Minnesota: prior restraint unconstitutional\n  1937  Court-packing failure → \"switch in time\"; expansion begins\n  1954  Brown v. Board: Thurgood Marshall; equal protection\n  1961  Mapp v. Ohio: 4th Amendment exclusionary rule → states\n  1963  Gideon v. Wainwright: right to counsel → states\n  1965  Griswold v. Connecticut: privacy (contraception)\n  1966  Miranda v. Arizona: 5th Amendment warnings\n  1971  Pentagon Papers: prior restraint unconstitutional\n  1972  Furman v. Georgia: death penalty (temporary halt)\n  1973  Roe v. Wade: abortion rights (1st trimester)\n  1996  Romer v. Evans: Ginsburg; gay rights\n  2003  Lawrence v. Texas: sodomy laws unconstitutional\n  2013  Shelby County v. Holder: VRA Section 4 gutted\n  2015  Obergefell v. Hodges: same-sex marriage\n  2022  Dobbs v. Jackson: Roe overturned\n```"
